some directors love to throw all kinds  of extra treats  into their movies for eagle-eyed fans  many of these are discovered in the days  and weeks after the movie's release  but others can go unnoticed for much  longer here are some extremely  well-hidden easter eggs that you might  have missed  the films of pixar animation boasts a  universe of easter eggs unto itself  the pizza planet truck from the first  pixar film toy story  traditionally makes a subtle appearance  in every movie from the studio  the code a113 is another classic  reference that continues to appear  throughout pixar films  it's a nod to a classroom number at cal  arts where many of the studio's  animators went to school  however some of the other easter eggs  are a bit harder to spot  recognize or even fully understand for  example  buried deep inside of toy story 4  there's a reference to the 2020 pixar  film onward  but it's a bit of a journey to discover  it we're going on a quest  the strange thing is that onward was  released nearly a year after toy story 4  hit theaters in june 2019.  it's an extremely tough easter egg to  notice but in the film  woody buzz lightyear and the whole gang  end up at a fair  later in a mid-credit scene there's a  wide shot of the fairgrounds and it  includes a bouncy castle with an  illustration of pegasus the mythical  wing creature  it's the exact same image as the one  painted on the side of the van used by  the two adventurous elf brothers in  onward  of course there's no way viewers could  have made this connection until a year  after toy story  4 was released bizarre supernatural  phenomena are  given in marvel films but the 2016 entry  doctor strange fully embraces the  weirdness  benedict cumberbatch stars as the title  character an extremely successful  surgeon  who stumbles into a world of magic  sorcery and sentient caves  in this mind-bending film there's  another dimension lurking past the  mundane reality of everyday life  also the climax of the movie involves a  vicious time loop  this is time endless  looped time both of those themes are  also explored in the classic  1993 comedy groundhog day in which bill  murray plays a narcissistic weatherman  caught in a punishing loop where  february 2nd repeats  over and over until he becomes a better  person  do you ever have deja vu mrs lancaster i  don't think so but i could check with  the kitchen  a fundamental philosophy isn't the only  thing linking the otherwise unrelated  films  there's an easter egg in doctor strange  that references groundhog day  on february 2nd 2018 the actual  groundhog day  twitter user tim d lydon noted that the  car accident that sets doctor strange on  his new adventure  occurs on february 2nd when we pause the  movie the date is visible on the  character's watch  doctor strange's director scott  derrickson weighed in on the easter egg  congratulating the viewer on the  discovery he tweeted i've waited two  years for somebody to notice this before  the marvel cinematic universe made  superhero movies the standard  director sam raimi wedded appetites for  comic book based films with his  spider-man trilogy in the 2000s  the first installment 2002 spider-man  tells the origin story of how nerdy teen  photographer peter parker  is having a hard time fitting in at  school everything changes on a field  trip when he's bitten by a radioactive  spider  he quickly develops superhuman abilities  and learns the tough way that with great  power comes great responsibility  by 2007 spider-man 3 peter's struggling  with his dual identity  and the pressures of being a superhero  on top of that  he has to deal with an alien symbiote  that has brought out his emo side  and completely altered any dance skills  that he might have previously possessed  but amongst all the action and angst  there's a tiny easter egg in the film  that goes all the way back to the  beginning of the trilogy  in a brief close-up of peter's right  hand there's a noticeable bump or scar  the telltale sign of a spider bite or in  this case  a radioactive spider bite although  considering how bad peter's hand looked  in the first film it's nothing he should  get too emotional about  it was the snap heard around the world  and arguably the most stunning  cliffhanger since luke skywalker found  out darth vader was his father at the  end of the empire strikes back  in avengers infinity war the  extraterrestrial villain thanos collects  all of the powerful infinity stones  from around the universe uses them to  kill or more precisely  wipe from existence half of all living  things  for a time that meant the heartbreaking  end for spider-man  dr strange black panther winter soldier  scarlet witch and most of the guardians  of the galaxy  among many others while the on-screen  deaths were shocking and tragic  few avengers fans thought all those  iconic heroes would stay dead for very  long  and indeed most of those deaths were  reversed in avengers end game  but marvel wasn't ready to show its  cards quite yet the rapid-fire marvel  studios logo that starts each mcu film  and which features the images of  numerous marvel characters  was altered for avengers end game all  the heroes who lost their lives to  thanos in infinity war were removed  it flew by on movie screens so quickly  that viewers didn't fully notice until  end game was released on home video  and super fans could examine every frame  whether they're films tv shows or video  games media aimed at kids have been used  as a launch pad for toys and  merchandising tie-ins for decades  and your friendly neighborhood  spider-man is no exception  in fact long before the mcu took over  theaters around the world  the wall crawler spawned all sorts of  non-comics products and some of them  were notoriously bad  case in point the spider-man popsicle  with gumball eyes  of course disappointment plus time often  equals nostalgia  when spider-man into the spider-verse  was released in 2019  it mined spidey memories of decades past  in all sorts of ways  some of these references were pretty  obvious while others were easy to miss  however one of these easter eggs is  almost impossible to catch because he  only shows up in a single frame  after peter parker's version of  spider-man lists some of his merchandise  he delivers a funny line about being a  so-so popsicle  then there's a quick shot of him getting  slammed by doc ock however there's one  frame in that segment where  thanks to doc ock's grip spidey's face  looks a lot like one of those  infamously misshapen treats check out  one of our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about  easter eggs are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

